var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"api.html#API-Reference","page":"API Reference","text":"GlobtimPlots is organized by what you want to draw:\n\nLevel sets — polynomial approximation contours with critical points overlaid (cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset, plot_polyapprox_levelset).\nConvergence & statistics — how approximation quality and recovered critical-point counts move with degree (plot_convergence_analysis, plot_discrete_l2).\nEigenvalue / Morse spectra — Hessian eigenvalues per critical point, colored by Morse type (plot_critical_eigenvalues, plot_all_eigenvalues).\nSubdivision — adaptive-partition diagnostics (plot_subdivision_partition, plot_subdivision_on_levelset, interactive_error_explorer).\n1D / 2D approximation — polynomial-fit-vs-truth plots (plot_1d_polynomial_approximation, plot_2d_partition).\n\nThe categorized index below complements the auto-generated docstrings.","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Choosing-a-backend","page":"API Reference","text":"GlobtimPlots draws through Makie. You must load a backend with using before calling any plot function — the backend-specific methods live in package extensions that activate on load:\n\nBackend Use for Notes\nCairoMakie Static, publication-quality PNG / PDF / SVG Powers all cairo_* functions and static plot_* output\nGLMakie Interactive 3D windows, animation, interactive_error_explorer Needs a display / GPU; not available headless\nWGLMakie Browser-embedded / Documenter-rendered interactive plots Used when embedding interactive figures in these docs\n\nusing GlobtimPlots\nusing CairoMakie     # load the backend FIRST\nfig = cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset(apol, ainp, df_cp, df_min)\nCairoMakie.save(\"levelset.png\", fig)","title":"Choosing a backend"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Worked-examples","page":"API Reference","text":"These mirror pkg/globtimplots/examples/gallery.jl, the script that regenerates the gallery images. Each assumes you have already built a Globtim approximation pol/TR and its critical-point DataFrames df_cp/df_min (see the Home page Quick Start).\n\nLevel set with critical points — cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset:\n\napol = adapt_polynomial_data(pol)\nainp = adapt_problem_input(TR)\nfig = cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset(\n    apol, ainp, df_cp, df_min;\n    chebyshev_levels = true,\n    title = \"Six-hump camel — polynomial level set (Chebyshev, d = 6)\",\n    xlabel = \"x₁\", ylabel = \"x₂\", colorbar_label = \"f(x)\",\n)\n\n(Image: Level set)\n\nAdaptive subdivision partition — plot_subdivision_partition (build a tree with adaptive_refine, then pass per-leaf bounds / L2 errors / degrees):\n\nfig = plot_subdivision_partition(\n    leaf_bounds, leaf_l2, leaf_deg;\n    title = \"Anisotropic subdivision  (color: log₁₀ L₂ error)\",\n    l2_tolerance = 0.005,\n    style = SubdivisionPartitionStyle(show_degree_labels = false),\n)\n\n(Image: Subdivision partition)\n\nDegree-sweep convergence — plot_convergence_analysis takes a results dictionary keyed by polynomial degree (each value carrying a .df of analyzed critical points) plus the degree range, and plots how the critical-point spread tightens with degree:\n\n# results :: Dict{Int} where results[d].df is the analyze_critical_points DataFrame at degree d\nfig = plot_convergence_analysis(results, 4, 14, 2)   # start, end, step\n\nThe gallery's combined L2-error-and-CP-count figure (shown below) is hand-built with Makie primitives in gallery.jl; adapt it when you want both axes on one plot.\n\n(Image: Convergence analysis)","title":"Worked examples"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Core-Functions","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Core Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#CairoMakie-Extension","page":"API Reference","text":"Static plotting functions for publication-quality output.","title":"CairoMakie Extension"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Level-Set-Plots","page":"API Reference","text":"cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset - Main level set visualization\nplot_polyapprox_levelset_2D - 2D level set variant","title":"Level Set Plots"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Statistical-Analysis","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_convergence_analysis - Convergence analysis plots  \nplot_discrete_l2 - L2 norm visualization\nplot_filtered_y_distances - Distance analysis\nplot_distance_statistics - Statistical distance plots\nplot_convergence_captured - Captured point analysis","title":"Statistical Analysis"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Eigenvalue-Analysis","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_hessian_norms - Hessian visualization\nplot_condition_numbers - Condition number plots\nplot_critical_eigenvalues - Eigenvalue analysis\nplot_all_eigenvalues - Complete eigenvalue spectrum\nplot_raw_vs_refined_eigenvalues - Refinement comparison","title":"Eigenvalue Analysis"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#GLMakie-Extension","page":"API Reference","text":"Interactive and 3D plotting functions.","title":"GLMakie Extension"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#3D-Visualization","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_polyapprox_3d - 3D surface visualization\nplot_polyapprox_levelset - Interactive level sets\nplot_level_set - Core level set plotting","title":"3D Visualization"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Animation","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_polyapprox_rotate - Rotation animations\nplot_polyapprox_animate - Animation sequences  \nplot_polyapprox_flyover - Flyover animations\nplot_polyapprox_animate2 - Advanced animations","title":"Animation"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Error-Visualization","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_error_function_1D_with_critical_points - 1D error visualization\nplot_error_function_2D_with_critical_points - 2D error visualization","title":"Error Visualization"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Subdivision-Visualization","page":"API Reference","text":"Functions for visualizing adaptive subdivision experiments.","title":"Subdivision Visualization"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Domain-Partition","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_subdivision_partition - 2D domain partition with convergence coloring, CPs, and degree labels\nSubdivisionPartitionStyle - Style configuration for partition plots","title":"Domain Partition"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Level-Set-Overlay","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_subdivision_on_levelset - Objective function contours with subdivision boundaries and CPs overlaid (tree-based; runtime only)\nplot_subdivision_on_levelset_from_bounds - Same plot built from serialized leaf bounds + L2 errors (works from JSON results, no tree needed)","title":"Level Set Overlay"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Error-Heatmap","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_subdivision_error_heatmap - Per-cell polynomial approximation error on a fine grid\ncompute_error_grid - Build error grid from tree and objective function\nfind_containing_leaf - Look up which leaf contains a query point","title":"Error Heatmap"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Interactive-Error-Explorer","page":"API Reference","text":"interactive_error_explorer - GLMakie zoom-refine explorer with reset and log/linear toggle","title":"Interactive Error Explorer"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Utilities","page":"API Reference","text":"format_degree_label - Format polynomial degree for display\neffective_degree - Compute effective degree from leaf data\nmin_degree - Minimum degree across leaves","title":"Utilities"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Subdivision-Tree","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_subdivision_tree - Tree structure visualization\nTreeVizStyle - Style configuration\nprint_tree_summary - Terminal summary","title":"Subdivision Tree"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#1D-Polynomial-Approximation","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_1d_polynomial_approximation - Plot 1D polynomial fit vs true function\nplot_1d_comparison - Compare multiple 1D fits","title":"1D Polynomial Approximation"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#2D-Partition-(AMR)","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_2d_partition - 2D AMR-style partition visualization\nplot_l2_trajectories - L2 error trajectory plots\nPartitionStyle - Style configuration","title":"2D Partition (AMR)"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Capture-Analysis","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_capture_convergence - Convergence of captured critical points\nplot_capture_sparsification_combined - Combined capture/sparsification plot","title":"Capture Analysis"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#Refinement-Trajectories","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_refinement_trajectories! - Overlay refinement paths on existing axes\nRefinementTrajectoryStyle - Style configuration","title":"Refinement Trajectories"},{"category":"section","location":"api.html#LV4D-Plots","page":"API Reference","text":"Lotka-Volterra 4D convergence and comparison plots.","title":"LV4D Plots"},{"category":"constant","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.CP_TYPE_TABLE","page":"API Reference","text":"CP_TYPE_TABLE\n\nCanonical named tuple mapping CP type keys (:min, :saddle, :max) to their visual appearance (color, marker, label).  All visualization code should use this table (or the cp_type_appearance helper) instead of defining local color/marker constants.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.CP_TYPE_TABLE"},{"category":"constant","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.PAPER_LINEWIDTH_UNITS","page":"API Reference","text":"\\linewidth of the manuscript (plain 10pt article: 345 pt) in Makie units (0.75 pt/unit).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.PAPER_LINEWIDTH_UNITS"},{"category":"constant","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.PAPER_PALETTE","page":"API Reference","text":"House palette: teal / red / orange / grey — matches the existing dcert/valley figures.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.PAPER_PALETTE"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.AbstractCriticalPointData","page":"API Reference","text":"AbstractCriticalPointData\n\nAbstract type for critical point data used in visualization.\n\nSubtypes should provide critical point locations and classifications for scatter plots and overlays.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.AbstractCriticalPointData"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.AbstractPolynomialData","page":"API Reference","text":"AbstractPolynomialData\n\nAbstract type for polynomial approximation data used in visualization.\n\nSubtypes should provide access to polynomial coefficients, basis information, and grid data needed for plotting level sets and surfaces.\n\nSee also: GenericPolynomialData, adapt_polynomial_data\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.AbstractPolynomialData"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.AbstractProblemInput","page":"API Reference","text":"AbstractProblemInput\n\nAbstract type for problem input data used in visualization.\n\nSubtypes should provide dimension, center, and domain range information needed for coordinate transformations in plots.\n\nSee also: GenericProblemInput, adapt_problem_input\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.AbstractProblemInput"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.BalancedTreeLayout","page":"API Reference","text":"BalancedTreeLayout\n\nCustom layout type for GraphMakie that uses split positions to determine child placement. Supports configurable horizontal scaling and vertical spacing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.BalancedTreeLayout"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.GenericPolynomialData","page":"API Reference","text":"GenericPolynomialData <: AbstractPolynomialData\n\nConcrete implementation of polynomial data for plotting.\n\nFields\n\ncoeffs::Any: Polynomial coefficients\nbasis::Symbol: Basis type (:chebyshev, :monomial, etc.), default :chebyshev\nscale_factor::Union{Float64, Vector{Float64}}: Domain scaling factor(s), default 1.0\ngrid::Matrix{Float64}: Evaluation grid points\nz::Vector{Float64}: Function values at grid points\nprecision::Any: Numerical precision information\nnormalized::Bool: Whether the approximation is normalized, default false\n\nSee also: AbstractPolynomialData, adapt_polynomial_data\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.GenericPolynomialData"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.GenericProblemInput","page":"API Reference","text":"GenericProblemInput <: AbstractProblemInput\n\nConcrete implementation of problem input data for plotting.\n\nFields\n\ndim::Int: Problem dimension (number of variables), default 2\ncenter::Vector{Float64}: Domain center point, default [0.0, 0.0]\nsample_range::Union{Float64, Vector{Float64}}: Domain sampling range(s), default 1.0\n\nSee also: AbstractProblemInput, adapt_problem_input\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.GenericProblemInput"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.PartitionStyle","page":"API Reference","text":"PartitionStyle\n\nStyling configuration for 2D partition visualization.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.PartitionStyle"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.PlotBackend","page":"API Reference","text":"PlotBackend\n\nEnum for plot backend selection.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.PlotBackend"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.RefinementTrajectoryStyle","page":"API Reference","text":"RefinementTrajectoryStyle\n\nVisual style for refinement trajectory overlays.\n\nFields\n\nlinewidth::Float64: Path line width (default 1.5)\nmarkersize_start::Float64: Start marker (circle) size (default 6.0)\nmarkersize_end::Float64: End marker (triangle) size (default 8.0)\nmarker_start::Symbol: Marker for raw CP (default :circle)\nmarker_end::Symbol: Marker for refined CP (default :dtriangle)\nstroke_color: Marker stroke color (default :black)\nstroke_width::Float64: Marker stroke width (default 0.5)\nline_alpha::Float64: Line opacity (default 0.8)\ncolors::Vector{Symbol}: Palette for trajectory coloring (cycled)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.RefinementTrajectoryStyle"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.SubdivisionPartitionStyle","page":"API Reference","text":"SubdivisionPartitionStyle\n\nStyling configuration for subdivision domain partition visualization. Controls colormap, degree labels, CP markers, convergence borders, colorbar, and legend.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.SubdivisionPartitionStyle"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo","page":"API Reference","text":"SubdomainNodeInfo\n\nExtracted information about a single subdomain node for visualization. Uses duck typing to work with Globtim's SubdivisionTree without hard dependency.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo"},{"category":"type","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.TreeVizStyle","page":"API Reference","text":"TreeVizStyle\n\nStyling configuration for subdivision tree visualization.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.TreeVizStyle"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._adaptive_spacing-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Real}}","page":"API Reference","text":"Compute adaptive spacing parameters from a set of x-axis positions.\n\nAll widths, offsets, and jitter scales derive from the actual data spacing, so plots automatically adapt to any x-axis values – whether evenly spaced polynomial degrees (4, 6, 8, 10) or non-uniform support sizes (70, 210, 495, 1001).\n\nReturns a NamedTuple with:\n\nmin_gap: minimum distance between adjacent positions\nfill_width: recommended total width for elements at a single position (~80% of min_gap)\njitter_scale: recommended scatter jitter magnitude (~10% of fill_width)\nlabel_offset: recommended horizontal offset for text labels beyond the last position\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._adaptive_spacing"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._apply_levelset_display_transform!-NTuple{4, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"_apply_levelset_display_transform!(raw_Z_ref, Z_display_obs, log_scale_obs, n_levels)\n\nApply log₁₀ transform (if enabled) to the raw Z grid and push result to the display observable.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._apply_levelset_display_transform!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._build_experiment_results_figure-Tuple{String, NamedTuple}","page":"API Reference","text":"_build_experiment_results_figure(experiment_name, metrics; fig_size) → Figure\n\nInternal: build the 4-panel experiment results figure using backend-agnostic Makie calls.  Both the interactive and static entry points delegate here.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._build_experiment_results_figure"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._build_legend_entries-Tuple{SubdivisionPartitionStyle}","page":"API Reference","text":"_build_legend_entries(style) → (entries, labels)\n\nBuild standard legend entries for CP types, convergence borders, and p*.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._build_legend_entries"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._build_levelset_base!-Tuple{Any, Globtim.SubdivisionTree, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"_build_levelset_base!(ax, tree, f; resolution, n_levels, colormap,\n                      l2_tolerance, cp_points, cp_types, p_true, style) → contourf_plot\n\nDraw the shared levelset base onto ax: filled contour of f, subdivision convergence boundaries, refined CPs, and p*. Returns the contourf! plot object for colorbar binding.\n\nDoes NOT draw raw CPs — callers handle raw CPs differently (static: _scatter_raw_cps!; interactive: named scatter for pick()).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._build_levelset_base!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._compute_dodge_offsets-Tuple{Int64, Float64}","page":"API Reference","text":"Compute horizontal offsets for dodged groups centered at 0.\n\nReturns a vector of offsets for each dodge group (1..ngroups), evenly distributed across [-totalwidth/2, +total_width/2].\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._compute_dodge_offsets"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._compute_error_grid_in_window-Tuple{Globtim.SubdivisionTree, Any, AbstractVector, AbstractVector}","page":"API Reference","text":"_compute_error_grid_in_window(tree, f, xs, ys) → Matrix{Float64}\n\nEvaluate |f(p) - poly(p)| on the grid defined by xs × ys. Returns raw (unscaled) error values; NaN for points outside any leaf or leaves without a polynomial.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._compute_error_grid_in_window"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._create_tree_legend!-Tuple{Any, Vector{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}, TreeVizStyle, Tuple{Float64, Float64}}","page":"API Reference","text":"_create_tree_legend!(fig, nodes, style, error_range)\n\nAdd legend to the figure showing dimension colors, leaf status, and error colorbar.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._create_tree_legend!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._domain_bbox-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"_domain_bbox(leaf_bounds) → (lo::Vector{Float64}, hi::Vector{Float64})\n\nCompute the axis-aligned bounding box of the domain from leaf bounds. leaf_bounds is Vector{Vector{Vector{Float64}}} — [leaf][dim] → [lo, hi].\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._domain_bbox"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._draw_boundary_segments!-Tuple{Any, Globtim.SubdivisionTree}","page":"API Reference","text":"_draw_boundary_segments!(ax, tree; color, linewidth)\n\nDraw subdomain boundary line segments for all leaves in the tree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._draw_boundary_segments!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._draw_convergence_boundaries!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"_draw_convergence_boundaries!(ax, leaf_bounds, leaf_l2_errors; l2_tolerance, style)\n\nDraw per-leaf boundary line segments colored by convergence status. Green for converged leaves (l2_error ≤ l2_tolerance), gray for unconverged.\n\nUses two batched linesegments! calls (one per status) for efficiency.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._draw_convergence_boundaries!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._draw_convergence_boundaries!-Tuple{Any, Globtim.SubdivisionTree}","page":"API Reference","text":"_draw_convergence_boundaries!(ax, tree::SubdivisionTree; l2_tolerance, style)\n\nTree-based dispatch: extracts leaf bounds and L2 errors from the tree, then delegates to the data-based method.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._draw_convergence_boundaries!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._draw_degree_labels!-NTuple{6, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"_draw_degree_labels!(ax, leaf_bounds, leaf_degrees, l2_errors, cmin, cmax; style)\n\nAnnotate degree inside each box with luminance-aware text color.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._draw_degree_labels!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._draw_partition_rects!-NTuple{5, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"_draw_partition_rects!(ax, leaf_bounds, l2_errors, cmin, cmax; style, l2_tolerance)\n\nDraw colored rectangles for leaf subdomains, colored by log₁₀(L2 error).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._draw_partition_rects!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._gradient_method_label-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"API Reference","text":"_gradient_method_label(method::Symbol) -> String\n\nHuman-readable label for the differentiation backend.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._gradient_method_label"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._gradient_method_short-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"API Reference","text":"_gradient_method_short(method::Symbol) -> String\n\nShort tag for log lines, e.g. \"[FD] \" or \"[AD] \". Includes trailing space so it concatenates cleanly with -> cp_type in log output.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._gradient_method_short"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._in_domain-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"_in_domain(p, lo, hi) → Bool\n\nCheck whether point p lies within the axis-aligned box [lo, hi].\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._in_domain"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._legend_kwargs-Tuple{}","page":"API Reference","text":"Standard legend styling kwargs.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._legend_kwargs"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._log_l2_colorrange-Tuple{Vararg{Vector{Float64}}}","page":"API Reference","text":"_log_l2_colorrange(error_vecs...) → (cmin, cmax)\n\nCompute a shared (cmin, cmax) color range from one or more vectors of L2 errors. Applies log10 and filters Inf/NaN.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._log_l2_colorrange"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._make_float_slider!-Tuple{Any, Int64, String, AbstractRange, Number}","page":"API Reference","text":"_make_float_slider!(layout, row, label_text, range, default_val, fmt)\n\nCreate a labeled slider with floating-point display format in layout[row, :]. Returns the Observable holding the slider value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._make_float_slider!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._make_info_button!-Tuple{Any, Int64, Int64, String, Observable}","page":"API Reference","text":"_make_info_button!(layout, row, col, tooltip, log_lines)\n\nCreate a small \"?\" button that logs tooltip to the log panel when clicked.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._make_info_button!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._make_linear_slider!-Tuple{Any, Int64, String, AbstractRange, Number}","page":"API Reference","text":"_make_linear_slider!(layout, row, label_text, range, default_val)\n\nCreate a labeled linear slider in layout[row, :]. Returns the Observable holding the slider value.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._make_linear_slider!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._make_log_slider!-Tuple{Any, Int64, String, AbstractRange, Number}","page":"API Reference","text":"_make_log_slider!(layout, row, label_text, exponent_range, default_exp)\n\nCreate a labeled log₁₀-scale slider in layout[row, :]. Returns the Observable holding the actual value (10^exponent).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._make_log_slider!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._plot_polyapprox_3d_impl-Tuple{AbstractPolynomialData, AbstractProblemInput, DataFrames.DataFrame, DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"_plot_polyapprox_3d_impl(pol, TR, df, df_min; kwargs...) -> Figure\n\nCore implementation of 3D polynomial approximation visualization. Returns a Figure with a 3D surface plot + critical point markers.\n\nBackend-agnostic: uses abstract Makie API (Figure, Axis3, surface!, scatter!). The GLMakie extension wraps this to add rotate animation support.\n\nArguments\n\npol::AbstractPolynomialData: Polynomial approximation data\nTR::AbstractProblemInput: Problem domain specification\ndf::DataFrame: All critical points (must have columns x1, x2, z; optional close for :proximity mode or critical_point_type for :hessian_type mode)\ndf_min::DataFrame: Minima points (must have columns x1, x2, value, captured)\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nfigure_size::Tuple{Int,Int}=(1000,800): Figure dimensions\nz_limits::Union{Nothing,Tuple{Float64,Float64}}=nothing: Z-axis limits (auto-computed if nothing)\nshow_captured::Bool=true: Whether to show captured minima markers\nalpha_surface::Float64=0.7: Surface transparency\nfade::Bool=false: Enable fade effect for top portion of z-range\nz_cut::Float64=0.25: Fraction of z-range to fade (when fade=true)\ncolor_by::Symbol=:proximity: How to color/group CP markers. :proximity (default) splits on df.close; :hessian_type groups by df.critical_point_type using CP_TYPE_TABLE palette + markers (min/saddle/max/degenerate).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._plot_polyapprox_3d_impl"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._prepare_contourf_args-Tuple{Matrix, Int64, SubdivisionPartitionStyle}","page":"API Reference","text":"_prepare_contourf_args(Z::Matrix, n_levels::Int, style) → (Z_display, levels_kw)\n\nApply optional log₁₀ transform and/or quantile-based level breaks to a raw objective grid Z.  Returns (Z_display, levels_kw) where levels_kw is either n_levels (Int) or a Vector{Float64} of explicit breakpoints.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._prepare_contourf_args"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._rank_positions-Tuple{AbstractVector{<:Integer}}","page":"API Reference","text":"Map non-uniform values to evenly-spaced rank positions (1, 2, 3, ...).\n\nWhen x-axis values have widely varying gaps (e.g., support sizes from binomial(n+d,d)), placing bars at literal values makes them vanishingly thin at the sparse end of the axis. Rank-based positioning gives uniform spacing while preserving the original values as tick labels.\n\nReturns (positions, ticks, value_to_rank) where:\n\npositions: rank-mapped vector (same length as input values)\nticks: (tick_positions, tick_labels) tuple for ax.xticks\nvalue_to_rank: Dict{Int, Int} mapping original values to rank positions\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._rank_positions"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._refine_error!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"_refine_error!(obs_state, ax; resolution)\n\nRe-sample the error grid at full resolution within the current zoom window of ax.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._refine_error!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._resolve_makie_backend-Tuple{PlotBackend}","page":"API Reference","text":"Resolve Makie backend module: CairoMakie for Static, GLMakie (loaded lazily) for Interactive.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._resolve_makie_backend"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._scatter_cps_by_type!-Tuple{Any, Vector, Vector}","page":"API Reference","text":"_scatter_cps_by_type!(ax, cp_points, cp_types; domain_lo, domain_hi, style)\n\nOverlay verified critical points colored by type (min/saddle/max). Points outside the domain are excluded when domain_lo and domain_hi are provided.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._scatter_cps_by_type!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._scatter_p_true!-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"_scatter_p_true!(ax, p_true; style)\n\nPlot the true parameter as a gold star.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._scatter_p_true!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._scatter_raw_cps!-Tuple{Any, Vector}","page":"API Reference","text":"_scatter_raw_cps!(ax, raw_cp_points; domain_lo, domain_hi, style)\n\nOverlay raw (pre-refinement) critical points as thin white crosses. Drawn before refined CPs so refined markers render on top.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._scatter_raw_cps!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots._variant_color_palette-Tuple{Int64}","page":"API Reference","text":"Build variant color palette: gray for Full (index 1), warm colors for sparsified variants.\n\nAll colors are returned as RGBAf with the given alpha baked in, ensuring consistent color types for CairoMakie rendering (no (color, alpha) tuple ambiguity).\n\nUses a slice of the :YlOrRd colormap starting at 40% to avoid near-white colors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots._variant_color_palette"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.adapt_polynomial_data-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"adapt_polynomial_data(globtim_poly) → GenericPolynomialData\n\nAdapt a polynomial approximation object to the GlobtimPlots plotting interface.\n\nThis function extracts common fields from polynomial types (like ApproxPoly from globtim) and wraps them in GenericPolynomialData which implements the AbstractPolynomialData interface.\n\nWhy Use This?\n\nThis adapter maintains clean package separation:\n\nglobtim defines concrete types (ApproxPoly) without depending on plotting packages\nglobtimplots defines abstract interfaces (AbstractPolynomialData)\nUsers explicitly convert when crossing package boundaries\n\nArguments\n\nglobtim_poly: Any object with polynomial approximation data (typically ApproxPoly)\n\nExtracted Fields\n\ncoeffs: Polynomial coefficients\nbasis: Basis type (:chebyshev, :monomial, etc.)\nscale_factor: Domain scaling factor\ngrid: Evaluation grid points (Matrix)\nz: Function values at grid points\nprecision: Numerical precision information\nnormalized: Whether the approximation is normalized\n\nReturns\n\nGenericPolynomialData <: AbstractPolynomialData: Wrapped data for plotting\n\nExample\n\nusing Globtim\nusing GlobtimPlots: adapt_polynomial_data\n\n# Create polynomial approximation in globtim\npol = ApproxPoly(...)\n\n# Adapt for plotting\npol_adapted = adapt_polynomial_data(pol)\n\n# Now can use with plotting functions\nfig = cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset(pol_adapted, ...)\n\nSee also: adapt_problem_input, GenericPolynomialData, AbstractPolynomialData\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.adapt_polynomial_data"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.adapt_problem_input-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"adapt_problem_input(globtim_input) → GenericProblemInput\n\nAdapt a problem input object to the GlobtimPlots plotting interface.\n\nThis function extracts common fields from problem input types (like TestInput from globtim) and wraps them in GenericProblemInput which implements the AbstractProblemInput interface.\n\nWhy Use This?\n\nThis adapter maintains clean package separation:\n\nglobtim defines concrete types (TestInput) without depending on plotting packages\nglobtimplots defines abstract interfaces (AbstractProblemInput)\nUsers explicitly convert when crossing package boundaries\n\nArguments\n\nglobtim_input: Any object with problem input data (typically TestInput)\n\nExtracted Fields\n\ndim: Problem dimension (number of variables)\ncenter: Domain center point (Vector)\nsample_range: Domain sampling range\n\nReturns\n\nGenericProblemInput <: AbstractProblemInput: Wrapped data for plotting\n\nExample\n\nusing Globtim\nusing GlobtimPlots: adapt_problem_input\n\n# Create problem input in globtim\nTR = TestInput(\n    f = x -> sum(x.^2),\n    dim = 2,\n    center = [0.0, 0.0],\n    sample_range = 2.0,\n    degree = 6\n)\n\n# Adapt for plotting\ntr_adapted = adapt_problem_input(TR)\n\n# Now can use with plotting functions\nfig = cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset(..., tr_adapted, ...)\n\nSee also: adapt_polynomial_data, GenericProblemInput, AbstractProblemInput\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.adapt_problem_input"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.analyze_captured_distances-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame, DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"Analyze distances between captured points and reference points. Returns statistics about minimum distances from each point in df to closest point in df_check.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.analyze_captured_distances"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.analyze_convergence_distances-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"Analyze convergence distances for a DataFrame of critical points. Returns statistics about the distances between points.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.analyze_convergence_distances"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.balanced_tree_layout-Tuple{Vector{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}, Int64}","page":"API Reference","text":"balanced_tree_layout(nodes::Vector{SubdomainNodeInfo}, root_id::Int; h_scale=10.0, v_spacing=1.5)\n\nCustom tree layout where horizontal child positions reflect split positions.\n\nSplit position p ∈ [-1,1] maps to:\n\nLeft child: positioned at relative offset -(1-p)/2  (closer to parent if split right)\nRight child: positioned at relative offset +(1+p)/2 (closer to parent if split left)\n\nThis visually shows WHERE in the domain each split occurred.\n\nArguments\n\nh_scale: Horizontal scaling factor (default 10.0) - spreads tree horizontally\nv_spacing: Vertical spacing between levels (default 1.5)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.balanced_tree_layout"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset-Tuple{AbstractPolynomialData, AbstractProblemInput, DataFrames.DataFrame, DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset(pol, TR, df, df_min; kwargs...)\n\nPlot polynomial approximation level sets with critical points overlaid.\n\nHandles per-coordinate scaling factors. Creates a CairoMakie contour plot with scattered critical points (near/far, captured/uncaptured).\n\nKeyword arguments\n\nfigure_size::Tuple{Int,Int} = (1000, 600): figure dimensions\nz_limits::Union{Nothing, Tuple{Float64,Float64}} = nothing: contour z range (auto if nothing)\nchebyshev_levels::Bool = false: use Chebyshev-spaced contour levels\nnum_levels::Int = 30: number of contour levels\nshow_captured::Bool = true: whether to show captured minima\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.compute_auto_scale-Tuple{Vector{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}, TreeVizStyle}","page":"API Reference","text":"compute_auto_scale(nodes::Vector{SubdomainNodeInfo}, style::TreeVizStyle) -> NamedTuple\n\nCompute scaling factors for nodes, fonts, and layout based on tree size. Returns named tuple with scaled values ready to use.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.compute_auto_scale"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.compute_error_grid-Tuple{Globtim.SubdivisionTree, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"compute_error_grid(tree::SubdivisionTree, f;\n                   resolution::Int = 200, log_scale::Bool = true)\n    → (xs, ys, error_matrix)\n\nEvaluate |f(p) - poly(p)| on a uniform grid over the tree's domain. Returns x-coordinates, y-coordinates, and the error matrix.\n\nIf log_scale, applies log10 to the error values (clamped to a minimum of 1e-20).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.compute_error_grid"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.compute_error_range-Tuple{Vector{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}}","page":"API Reference","text":"compute_error_range(nodes::Vector{SubdomainNodeInfo}) -> Tuple{Float64,Float64}\n\nCompute min/max error range for active leaves (used for error gradient coloring).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.compute_error_range"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.compute_error_reduction-Tuple{Vector{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}, GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}","page":"API Reference","text":"compute_error_reduction(nodes, node::SubdomainNodeInfo) -> Union{Float64,Nothing}\n\nCompute percentage error reduction from this node to its children. Returns Nothing for leaf nodes or if children have Inf error.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.compute_error_reduction"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.compute_figure_size-Tuple{Vector{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}, TreeVizStyle}","page":"API Reference","text":"compute_figure_size(nodes::Vector{SubdomainNodeInfo}, style::TreeVizStyle) -> Tuple{Int,Int}\n\nCalculate optimal figure size based on tree structure.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.compute_figure_size"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.cp_type_appearance-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"API Reference","text":"cp_type_appearance(cp_type) → (color::Symbol, marker::Symbol)\n\nLook up color and marker for a CP type (Symbol or String). Accepts both short (:min) and long (:minimum) key forms. Returns (:magenta, :diamond) for unknown types.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.cp_type_appearance"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_approximation_plot!-Tuple{Any, Any, Dict, String}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_approximation_plot!(gridpos, Makie, stats::Dict, title::String)\n\nPlot L2 approximation error vs degree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_approximation_plot!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_campaign_comparison_plot-Tuple{Any, Dict}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_campaign_comparison_plot(campaign, stats::Vector; backend::PlotBackend=Static) -> Figure or Vector{Figure}\n\nCreate comparison plots across multiple experiments in a campaign. For Interactive backend, returns a vector of separate figures (one per window). For Static backend, returns a single combined figure.\n\nWorks with any campaign object that has the field: experiments. Typically used with CampaignResults from GlobtimPostProcessing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_campaign_comparison_plot"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_convergence_trajectory_plot!-Tuple{Any, Any, Dict, String}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_convergence_trajectory_plot!(gridpos, Makie, stats::Dict, title::String)\n\nPlot convergence trajectories showing improvement rates across degrees.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_convergence_trajectory_plot!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_critical_points_plot!-Tuple{Any, Any, Dict, String}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_critical_points_plot!(gridpos, Makie, stats::Dict, title::String)\n\nPlot critical point counts vs degree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_critical_points_plot!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_experiment_plots-Tuple{Any, Dict}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_experiment_plots(result, stats::Dict; backend::PlotBackend=Static) -> Figure\n\nCreate adaptive plots based on available tracking labels.\n\nWorks with any result object that has the fields: enabledtracking, experimentid, metadata. Typically used with ExperimentResult from GlobtimPostProcessing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_experiment_plots"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_level_set_animation-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Any, Array{StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, T}, 3}, Union{Nothing, DataFrames.DataFrame}, Tuple{T, T}}, Tuple{Any, Array{StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, T}, 3}, Union{Nothing, DataFrames.DataFrame}, Tuple{T, T}, VisualizationParameters{T}}} where T<:AbstractFloat","page":"API Reference","text":"create_level_set_animation(\n    f,\n    grid::Array{SVector{3,T},3},\n    df::Union{DataFrame,Nothing},\n    z_range::Tuple{T,T},\n    params::VisualizationParameters{T} = VisualizationParameters{T}();\n    fps::Int = 30,\n    duration::Int = 20,\n    output_file::String = \"level_set_animation.mp4\"\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nCreate an animated level set visualization that sweeps through levels while rotating the camera.\n\nArguments\n\nf: Objective function\ngrid: 3D array of sample points\ndf: Optional DataFrame with critical points\nz_range: Range of level values to animate\nparams: Visualization parameters\nfps: Frames per second for animation\nduration: Animation duration in seconds\noutput_file: Path to save the animation\n\nReturns\n\nGLMakie Figure object\n\nExample\n\nfig = create_level_set_animation(\n    f, grid, df, (-3.0, 6.0);\n    fps = 30,\n    duration = 10,\n    output_file = \"my_animation.mp4\"\n)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_level_set_animation"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_level_set_animation-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Array{T}, Array{StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, T}, 3}, Union{Nothing, DataFrames.DataFrame}, Tuple{T, T}}, Tuple{Array{T}, Array{StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, T}, 3}, Union{Nothing, DataFrames.DataFrame}, Tuple{T, T}, VisualizationParameters{T}}} where T<:AbstractFloat","page":"API Reference","text":"create_level_set_animation(\n    values::Array{T},\n    grid::Array{SVector{3,T},3},\n    df::Union{DataFrame,Nothing},\n    z_range::Tuple{T,T},\n    params::VisualizationParameters{T} = VisualizationParameters{T}();\n    fps::Int = 30,\n    duration::Int = 20,\n    output_file::String = \"level_set_animation.mp4\"\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nCreate an animated level set visualization from pre-computed grid values.\n\nSame as the f-based overload, but skips function evaluation — uses the provided values array directly. The values array must have the same shape as grid.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_level_set_animation"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_level_set_visualization-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Any, Array{StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, T}, 3}, Union{Nothing, DataFrames.DataFrame}, Tuple{T, T}}, Tuple{Any, Array{StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, T}, 3}, Union{Nothing, DataFrames.DataFrame}, Tuple{T, T}, VisualizationParameters{T}}} where T<:AbstractFloat","page":"API Reference","text":"create_level_set_visualization(\n    f,\n    grid::Array{SVector{3,T},3},\n    df::Union{DataFrame,Nothing},\n    z_range::Tuple{T,T},\n    params::VisualizationParameters{T} = VisualizationParameters{T}()\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nCreate an interactive 3D level set visualization with a slider.\n\nArguments\n\nf: Objective function to visualize\ngrid: 3D array of sample points\ndf: Optional DataFrame with critical points (columns: x1, x2, x3, z)\nz_range: Tuple (min, max) for level values\nparams: Visualization parameters\n\nReturns\n\nGLMakie Figure with interactive slider\n\nExample\n\nusing GLMakie, StaticArrays, GlobtimPlots\n\n# Create a simple test function\nf(x) = x[1]^2 + x[2]^2 + x[3]^2\n\n# Create grid\ngrid = [SVector{3,Float64}(x, y, z)\n        for x in range(-1, 1, 50),\n            y in range(-1, 1, 50),\n            z in range(-1, 1, 50)]\n\n# Visualize\nfig = create_level_set_visualization(f, grid, nothing, (0.0, 3.0))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_level_set_visualization"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_level_set_visualization-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Array{T}, Array{StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, T}, 3}, Union{Nothing, DataFrames.DataFrame}, Tuple{T, T}}, Tuple{Array{T}, Array{StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, T}, 3}, Union{Nothing, DataFrames.DataFrame}, Tuple{T, T}, VisualizationParameters{T}}} where T<:AbstractFloat","page":"API Reference","text":"create_level_set_visualization(\n    values::Array{T},\n    grid::Array{SVector{3,T},3},\n    df::Union{DataFrame,Nothing},\n    z_range::Tuple{T,T},\n    params::VisualizationParameters{T} = VisualizationParameters{T}()\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nCreate an interactive 3D level set visualization from pre-computed grid values.\n\nSame as the f-based overload, but skips function evaluation — uses the provided values array directly. The values array must have the same shape as grid.\n\nInf and NaN entries in values are treated as missing (excluded from level sets).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_level_set_visualization"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_parameter_recovery_plot!-Tuple{Any, Any, Dict, String}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_parameter_recovery_plot!(gridpos, Makie, stats::Dict, title::String)\n\nPlot parameter recovery error vs degree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_parameter_recovery_plot!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_residual_distribution_plot!-Tuple{Any, Any, Dict, String}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_residual_distribution_plot!(gridpos, Makie, stats::Dict, title::String)\n\nPlot histogram of residuals/errors to show distribution quality.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_residual_distribution_plot!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_single_plot-Tuple{Any, Dict, Symbol, String}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_single_plot(result, stats::Dict, plot_type::Symbol, title::String; backend::PlotBackend=Interactive) -> Figure\n\nCreate a single plot window for a specific plot type.\n\nWorks with any result object that has the relevant fields for the specified plot_type. Typically used with ExperimentResult from GlobtimPostProcessing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_single_plot"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_stability_plot!-Tuple{Any, Any, Dict, String}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_stability_plot!(gridpos, Makie, stats::Dict, title::String)\n\nPlot condition numbers vs degree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_stability_plot!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_timing_plot!-Tuple{Any, Any, Dict, String}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_timing_plot!(gridpos, Makie, stats::Dict, title::String)\n\nPlot timing breakdown by degree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_timing_plot!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.create_training_dashboard-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"create_training_dashboard(run; size=(1600, 1200))\n\nCreate comprehensive dashboard with all training plots\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.create_training_dashboard"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.draw_depth_bands!-Tuple{Any, Vector{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}, Vector{Point{2, Float64}}, TreeVizStyle}","page":"API Reference","text":"draw_depth_bands!(ax, nodes, positions, style)\n\nDraw alternating horizontal bands at each tree depth for visual hierarchy.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.draw_depth_bands!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.effective_degree-Tuple{Integer}","page":"API Reference","text":"effective_degree(d) → Int\n\nEffective (maximum) degree: scalar as-is, vector → maximum(d).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.effective_degree"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.extract_tree_data-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"extract_tree_data(tree) -> (Vector{SubdomainNodeInfo}, Set{Int}, Set{Int}, Int)\n\nExtract node information from a SubdivisionTree using duck typing. Returns node info vector, converged leaf IDs, active leaf IDs, and root_id.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.extract_tree_data"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.find_containing_leaf-Tuple{Globtim.SubdivisionTree, AbstractVector{Float64}}","page":"API Reference","text":"find_containing_leaf(tree::SubdivisionTree, point::AbstractVector{Float64}) → Subdomain\n\nFind the leaf subdomain containing point. Errors if no leaf contains the point.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.find_containing_leaf"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.fit_linear_trend-Tuple{Vector, Vector}","page":"API Reference","text":"Helper function to fit linear trend\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.fit_linear_trend"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.format_degree_label-Tuple{Integer}","page":"API Reference","text":"format_degree_label(d) → String\n\nFormat a degree value for display: scalar 4 → \"4\", vector [4,8] → \"(4,8)\".\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.format_degree_label"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.format_node_label-Tuple{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo, Vector{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}, TreeVizStyle}","page":"API Reference","text":"format_node_label(node::SubdomainNodeInfo, nodes::Vector{SubdomainNodeInfo}, style::TreeVizStyle; balanced_layout::Bool=true) -> String\n\nFormat node label for display. When balancedlayout is true, split position is encoded in edge lengths so we skip the ASCII viz. Labels are truncated to style.labelmax_chars.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.format_node_label"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.format_param_value-Tuple{String, Any, String}","page":"API Reference","text":"format_param_value(param_name::String, value::Any, prefix::String) -> String\n\nFormat a parameter value for display in labels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.format_param_value"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.generate_experiment_labels-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"generate_experiment_labels(campaign) -> Vector{String}\n\nGenerate concise, informative labels for experiments in a campaign. Automatically detects which parameter varies and creates labels accordingly.\n\nArguments\n\ncampaign: Campaign results object with .experiments field\n\nStrategy\n\nIdentify which parameters vary across experiments\nIf only one parameter varies, label by that parameter value\nIf multiple parameters vary, create compact multi-parameter labels\nHandle common parameter types (domainsizeparam, parameter_set, etc.)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.generate_experiment_labels"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.get_dim_color-Tuple{Int64, TreeVizStyle}","page":"API Reference","text":"get_dim_color(dim::Int, style::TreeVizStyle)\n\nGet color for a dimension, cycling through available colors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.get_dim_color"},{"category":"function","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.get_node_color","page":"API Reference","text":"get_node_color(node::SubdomainNodeInfo, style::TreeVizStyle, error_range::Tuple{Float64,Float64})\n\nDetermine node color based on node type, with error gradient for active leaves.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.get_node_color"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.get_node_marker-Tuple{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}","page":"API Reference","text":"get_node_marker(node::SubdomainNodeInfo) -> Symbol\n\nDetermine node marker shape based on node type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.get_node_marker"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.get_node_size-Tuple{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo, TreeVizStyle}","page":"API Reference","text":"get_node_size(node::SubdomainNodeInfo, style::TreeVizStyle) -> Float64\n\nGet node size based on type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.get_node_size"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.get_param_label_prefix-Tuple{String}","page":"API Reference","text":"get_param_label_prefix(param_name::String) -> String\n\nGet a human-readable prefix for a parameter name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.get_param_label_prefix"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.getfield_or_index-Tuple{Any, Symbol}","page":"API Reference","text":"Helper to get field from struct or NamedTuple by symbol. Works with both field access and getindex for Dict-like objects.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.getfield_or_index"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.interactive_error_explorer-Tuple{Globtim.SubdivisionTree, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"interactive_error_explorer(\n    tree::SubdivisionTree, f;\n    resolution::Int = 200,\n    log_scale::Bool = true,\n    colormap::Symbol = :viridis,\n) → Figure\n\nLaunch an interactive GLMakie window showing |f(p) - poly(p)| across the subdivision domain. Requires GLMakie to be loaded and active.\n\nInteraction\n\nZoom into a region with the mouse scroll / drag\n\"Refine View\" re-renders at full resolution within the current zoom window\n\"Reset\" restores the full domain view\n\"Toggle log/linear\" switches between log₁₀ and raw error display (instant, no recompute)\n\nArguments\n\ntree: SubdivisionTree with populated polynomials (runtime only)\nf: Objective function f(x::Vector{Float64}) → Float64\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nresolution: Grid points per axis (default 200)\nlog_scale: Start with log₁₀ scale (default true)\ncolormap: Makie colormap (default :viridis)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.interactive_error_explorer"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.interactive_levelset_explorer-Tuple{Any, Vector}","page":"API Reference","text":"interactive_levelset_explorer(\n    f, bounds::Vector;\n    refine_newton::Function,\n    refine_optim::Function,\n    leaf_bounds::Vector,\n    leaf_l2_errors::Vector{Float64},\n    raw_cp_points::Vector = Vector{Float64}[],\n    cp_points::Vector = Vector{Float64}[],\n    cp_types::Vector = String[],\n    p_true = nothing,\n    l2_tolerance::Union{Nothing, Float64} = nothing,\n    resolution::Int = 200,\n    n_levels::Int = 30,\n    colormap::Symbol = :viridis,\n    style::SubdivisionPartitionStyle = SubdivisionPartitionStyle(),\n    title::String = \"Interactive Levelset Explorer\",\n) → Vector{Figure}\n\nLaunch an interactive GLMakie explorer as two windows: a plot window (axis + colorbar) and a controls window (buttons + log panel). This avoids layout conflicts between DataAspect() and fixed-height controls that cause vertical size constraints on macOS.\n\nShows the objective function as a filled contour with subdivision boundaries overlaid. Right-click raw critical points (white crosses) to select/deselect them, then click \"Refine Selected\" to batch-refine all selected CPs.\n\nInteraction\n\nRight-click a raw CP → toggle selection (highlighted in yellow)\nRefine Selected (N) batch-refines all selected CPs, draws trajectories + markers\nRefine: dropdown menu selects refinement mode (Newton ∇f=0 or Optim f-min)\nLog₁₀ toggle switch enables/disables log₁₀ scale on the contour\nLevels slider adjusts contour density (5–100 levels)\nClear removes all refined markers, trajectories, and selection\nRefine View re-evaluates the contour at full resolution within the current zoom window\nReset returns to the full domain view\n\nKeyboard shortcuts (plot window)\n\nKey Action\nr Refine Selected\nc Clear Refined\nv Refine View\nz Reset View\nl Toggle Log₁₀\n\nCallback contract\n\nBoth refine_newton and refine_optim must accept (point::Vector{Float64}; kwargs...) and return a NamedTuple with fields:\n\n(; point::Vector{Float64}, objective_value::Float64, gradient_norm::Float64,\n   cp_type::Symbol, converged::Bool, iterations::Int, trace::Vector{Vector{Float64}})\n\nKeyword arguments forwarded from sliders:\n\nNewton: tol, accept_tol, max_iterations, hessian_tol, trust_radius_fraction\nOptim: f_abstol, x_abstol, max_iterations, hessian_tol, method (:neldermead or :lbfgs), step_size (LBFGS only)\n\nArguments\n\nf: Objective function f(x::Vector{Float64}) → Float64\nbounds: Domain bounds as [collect(dim1_bounds), collect(dim2_bounds)]\nrefine_newton: Callback for trust-region Newton on ∇f=0 (all CP types)\nrefine_optim: Callback for NelderMead f-minimization\nleaf_bounds: Per-leaf domain bounds from subdivision\nleaf_l2_errors: Per-leaf L2 approximation errors\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nraw_cp_points: Raw (pre-refinement) critical points — pickable targets\ncp_points, cp_types: Already-refined CPs and their types\np_true: True parameter vector (gold star)\nl2_tolerance: For convergence border coloring\nresolution: Grid points per axis for contour evaluation\nn_levels: Number of contour levels\ncolormap: Colormap for filled contour\nstyle: SubdivisionPartitionStyle for marker/border styling\ntitle: Plot title\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.interactive_levelset_explorer"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.interactive_levelset_explorer-Tuple{Globtim.SubdivisionTree, Function}","page":"API Reference","text":"interactive_levelset_explorer(\n    tree::SubdivisionTree, f;\n    refine_newton::Function,\n    refine_optim::Function,\n    kwargs...\n) → Vector{Figure}\n\nTree-based overload — extracts bounds, leafbounds, and leafl2_errors from the tree, then delegates to the data-based method.\n\nReturns [plot_fig, controls_fig] (two separate windows).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.interactive_levelset_explorer"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.min_degree-Tuple{Integer}","page":"API Reference","text":"min_degree(d) → Int\n\nMinimum degree: scalar as-is, vector → minimum(d).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.min_degree"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.normalize_cp_key-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"API Reference","text":"normalize_cp_key(k::Symbol) → Symbol\n\nNormalize verbose CP type keys to the canonical short form used by CP_TYPE_TABLE:  :minimum → :min,  :maximum → :max. All other keys pass through unchanged.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.normalize_cp_key"},{"category":"function","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.paper_figsize","page":"API Reference","text":"paper_figsize(fraction = 1.0; aspect = 0.55) -> (w, h)\n\nFigure size in Makie units for a figure included at fraction * \\linewidth. aspect is height/width. Author at this size and include at the SAME fraction so page font sizes equal the theme's sizes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.paper_figsize"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.paper_theme-Tuple{}","page":"API Reference","text":"paper_theme(; fontsize = 12) -> Theme\n\nShared manuscript theme. fontsize 12 Makie units = 9 pt on the page (ticks one step smaller). Colormap :viridis everywhere; palette PAPER_PALETTE.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.paper_theme"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_1d_comparison-Tuple{Function, Dict{Int64, <:NamedTuple}}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_1d_comparison(\n    f::Function,\n    results::Dict{Int, NamedTuple};\n    poly_eval_factory::Function,\n    n_plot_points::Int = 500,\n    figsize::Tuple{Int, Int} = (1200, 400),\n    save_path::Union{String, Nothing} = nothing\n) -> Figure\n\nCreate a multi-panel comparison figure showing polynomial approximations at different degrees.\n\nArguments\n\nf: Original function (scalar input, scalar output)\nresults: Dict mapping degree => (poly=..., df=..., TR=...) NamedTuple\npoly_eval_factory: Function that takes a poly and returns evaluation function: poly -> (xi -> evaluate(poly, [xi]))\nfunc_latex: LaTeX string for function label in legend (default: \"Original f(x)\")\nn_samples: Number of sample points used in construction (shown in legend)\n\nReturns\n\nFigure: CairoMakie Figure with one panel per degree\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_1d_comparison"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_1d_polynomial_approximation-Tuple{Function, Any, DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_1d_polynomial_approximation(\n    f::Function,\n    poly,\n    critical_points::DataFrame;\n    poly_eval::Function = nothing,\n    n_plot_points::Int = 500,\n    title::String = \"1D Polynomial Approximation\",\n    show_l2_error::Bool = true,\n    save_path::Union{String, Nothing} = nothing,\n    figsize::Tuple{Int, Int} = (800, 600)\n) -> Figure\n\nPlot a 1D function with its polynomial approximation and critical points.\n\nArguments\n\nf: Original function (scalar input, scalar output)\npoly: ApproxPoly object from globtim (used for metadata: center, scale_factor, nrm, degree)\ncritical_points: DataFrame with x1 and z columns from process_crit_pts\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\npoly_eval: Function to evaluate polynomial at a point x -> evaluate(poly, [x]). Required.\nn_plot_points: Number of points for smooth curve plotting (default: 500)\ntitle: Plot title\nshow_l2_error: Whether to annotate L2 approximation error (default: true)\nfunc_latex: LaTeX string for function label in legend (default: \"Original f(x)\")\nn_samples: Number of sample points used in construction (shown as annotation)\nsave_path: If provided, save figure to this path\nfigsize: Figure size in pixels (default: (800, 600))\n\nReturns\n\nFigure: CairoMakie Figure object\n\nExample\n\nusing Globtim, GlobtimPlots, DynamicPolynomials, DataFrames\n\nf = x -> 0.5 * (x^4 - 16*x^2 + 5*x)\nTR = TestInput(f, dim=1, center=[0.0], sample_range=5.0, GN=16)\npoly = Constructor(TR, 12)\n\n@polyvar x\nsolutions = solve_polynomial_system(x, poly)\ndf = process_crit_pts(solutions, f, TR)\n\nfig = plot_1d_polynomial_approximation(\n    f, poly, df,\n    poly_eval = xi -> evaluate(poly, [xi]),\n    title = \"Styblinski-Tang 1D\"\n)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_1d_polynomial_approximation"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_2d_partition-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_2d_partition(subdomains; kwargs...)\n\nPlot 2D subdomain partition on domain [-1,1]².\n\nArguments\n\nsubdomains: Iterable of objects with fields center, half_widths, l2_error, degree, id\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\ncolor_by::Symbol = :l2_error: Color by :l2_error (log scale) or :degree\ntitle::String = \"Domain Partition\": Plot title\nstyle::PartitionStyle = PartitionStyle(): Styling configuration\nfig = nothing: Existing Figure to plot into (creates new if nothing)\nax = nothing: Existing Axis to plot into (creates new if nothing)\n\nReturns\n\nFigure: The Makie figure\n\nExample\n\n# Collect subdomains from episode\nfinal_subs = collect_final_subdomains(env)\n\n# Plot colored by L2 error\nfig = plot_2d_partition(final_subs, color_by=:l2_error, title=\"AdaptiveL2 Policy\")\nsave(\"partition.pdf\", fig)\n\n# Plot colored by degree\nfig = plot_2d_partition(final_subs, color_by=:degree, title=\"Polynomial Degrees\")\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_2d_partition"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_action_distribution-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_action_distribution(run; size=(1000, 600))\n\nPlot action distribution across episodes as stacked bar chart or heatmap\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_action_distribution"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_action_ratio_evolution-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_action_ratio_evolution(run; fig_size=(1000, 600))\n\nPlot the ratio of SUBDIVIDE to INCREASE_DEGREE actions across episodes. Shows whether agent learns to prefer subdivision or degree increases.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_action_ratio_evolution"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_action_stacked_area-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_action_stacked_area(run; fig_size=(1000, 600))\n\nStacked area plot showing the proportion of different actions across episodes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_action_stacked_area"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_all_eigenvalues-Tuple{Function, DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_all_eigenvalues(f, df; sort_by=:magnitude, fig_size=nothing)\n\nComplete eigenvalue spectrum visualization separated by critical-point type, with multiple sort options (:magnitude, :abs_magnitude, :smallest, :largest, :spread, :index).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_all_eigenvalues"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_capture_convergence-Tuple{Vector{Tuple{Int64, GlobtimPostProcessing.CaptureResult}}, GlobtimPostProcessing.KnownCriticalPoints}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_capture_convergence(\n    degree_capture_results::Vector{Tuple{Int, CaptureResult}},\n    known::KnownCriticalPoints;\n    fig_size = (900, 900),\n    l2_errors = nothing,\n    show_l2 = false,\n    support_sizes = nothing,\n    save_path = nothing,\n) -> Figure\n\nCreate a multi-panel figure showing capture analysis convergence.\n\nWhen support_sizes is provided, the x-axis shows the number of nonzero polynomial coefficients (support size) instead of polynomial degree. All spacing and bar widths adapt automatically to the data via _adaptive_spacing.\n\nPanels (top to bottom)\n\nDistance distribution: One sub-panel per CP type (min/max/saddle), each with its own y-range and log y-scale. Boxplots + jittered scatter of distances from each known CP to its nearest computed CP. Horizontal dashed lines at tolerance levels.\nCapture rate: Grouped bars showing fraction of known CPs captured at each tolerance level.\nL2 approximation error (optional): Only shown when both l2_errors data is provided AND show_l2=true. Not displayed by default.\n\nArguments\n\ndegree_capture_results: Vector of (degree, CaptureResult) tuples, one per degree. All CaptureResults must use the same tolerance_fractions.\nknown: KnownCriticalPoints with the ground truth.\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nfig_size: Figure dimensions in pixels.\nl2_errors: Optional Vector{Tuple{Int, Float64}} of (degree, l2_error) pairs.\nshow_l2: Whether to display the L2 error panel. Default false. Requires l2_errors to be provided as well.\nsupport_sizes: Optional Dict{Int, Int} mapping degree -> support size (nonzero coefficients). When provided, x-axis shows support size instead of degree.\nsave_path: Optional file path to save the figure (e.g., \"capture_convergence.png\").\n\nReturns\n\nFigure: CairoMakie figure object.\n\nExample\n\nusing GlobtimPlots, GlobtimPostProcessing\n\n# With support size on x-axis\nsupport_sizes = Dict(dr.degree => dr.support_size\n    for dr in degree_results if dr.status == \"success\")\nfig = plot_capture_convergence(\n    degree_capture_results, known_cps;\n    support_sizes = support_sizes,\n    l2_errors = [(dr.degree, dr.l2_approx_error) for dr in degree_results if dr.status == \"success\"],\n)\ndisplay(fig)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_capture_convergence"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_capture_sparsification_combined-Tuple{Vector{<:NamedTuple}, GlobtimPostProcessing.KnownCriticalPoints}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_capture_sparsification_combined(\n    entries,\n    known::KnownCriticalPoints;\n    fig_size = (1400, 700),\n    save_path = nothing,\n) -> Figure\n\nTwo-panel side-by-side figure showing the sparsification speed vs accuracy tradeoff.\n\nThe x-axis uses support size (number of nonzero coefficients) from the Full variant at each degree, so the axis reflects actual polynomial complexity. All spacing and bar widths adapt automatically via _adaptive_spacing.\n\nPanel A (left) – CP Accuracy: Distance to Known CPs\n\nStacked per-type subpanels with dodged boxplots for each support size x variant. Log-y scale, tolerance reference lines. Shows how much CP accuracy degrades with sparsification.\n\nPanel B (right) – HC Solve Time\n\nGrouped bar chart: x-axis = support size, bars dodged by variant. Y-axis = solve time (seconds). Each sparsified bar is annotated with absolute time saved. Shows how much faster the HC solve is with sparsification.\n\nArguments\n\nentries: Vector of NamedTuples, each with fields:\ndegree::Int – polynomial degree\nvariant_label::String – \"Full\", \"1e-5 (mild)\", etc.\nthreshold::Float64 – sparsification threshold (0.0 for full polynomial)\ncapture_result::CaptureResult – full capture analysis\nn_nonzero_coeffs::Int – number of non-zero coefficients\nl2_ratio::Float64 – ratio of sparsified L2 norm to original (1.0 for full)\nsolve_time::Float64 – HC solve wall-clock time in seconds\nknown::KnownCriticalPoints: Ground truth critical points.\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nfig_size: Figure dimensions in pixels.\nsave_path: Optional file path to save the figure.\n\nReturns\n\nFigure: CairoMakie figure object.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_capture_sparsification_combined"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_condition_numbers-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_condition_numbers(df; fig_size=(800,600))\n\nLog-scale scatter plot of Hessian condition numbers κ(H) = |λmax|/|λmin|.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_condition_numbers"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_convergence_analysis-Tuple{Any, Int64, Int64, Int64}","page":"API Reference","text":"Plot summary of convergence distances for a range of degrees –> for each captured \"x\", compute the distance to \"y\", the optimized point.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_convergence_analysis"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_critical_eigenvalues-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_critical_eigenvalues(df; fig_size=(1200,500))\n\nTwo-panel plot: smallest positive eigenvalues (minima) and largest negative eigenvalues (maxima).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_critical_eigenvalues"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_discrete_l2-Tuple{Any, Int64, Int64, Int64}","page":"API Reference","text":"Plot the discrete L2-norm approximation error attained by the polynomial approximant.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_discrete_l2"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_distance_statistics-Tuple{Dict{String, Any}}","page":"API Reference","text":"Plot the outputs ofanalyze_converged_points function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_distance_statistics"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_episode_decision_timeline-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_episode_decision_timeline(episode_metrics, state_action_history; fig_size=(1200, 600))\n\nPlot the sequence of decisions made during a single episode. Shows when SUBDIVIDE vs INCREASE_DEGREE was chosen and in what state.\n\nArguments\n\nepisode_metrics: Metrics for the episode (any object with episode info)\nstate_action_history: Vector of (step, state, action) tuples from the episode\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_episode_decision_timeline"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_experiment_results_interactive-Tuple{String, NamedTuple}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_experiment_results_interactive(experiment_name, metrics; fig_size)\n\nCreate interactive window showing experiment results. Delegates to the shared figure builder, then calls display.\n\nParameters:\n\nexperiment_name: Name of experiment for title\nmetrics: NamedTuple with fields: degrees, l2norms, mindistances, meandistances, conditionnumbers\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_experiment_results_interactive"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_experiment_results_static-Tuple{String, NamedTuple}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_experiment_results_static(experiment_name, metrics; output_file, fig_size)\n\nCreate static PNG/PDF/SVG plot and save to file.\n\nParameters:\n\nexperiment_name: Name of experiment for title\nmetrics: NamedTuple with fields: degrees, l2norms, mindistances, meandistances, conditionnumbers\noutput_file: Path to save file (extension determines format: .png, .pdf, .svg)\n\nReturns:\n\nPath to saved file\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_experiment_results_static"},{"category":"function","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_filtered_y_distances","page":"API Reference","text":"Updated plotfilteredy_distances function to handle per-coordinate scaling.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_filtered_y_distances"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_hessian_norms-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_hessian_norms(df; fig_size=(800,600))\n\nScatter plot of Hessian Frobenius norms, colored by critical-point type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_hessian_norms"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_l2_convergence_trials-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_l2_convergence_trials(df::DataFrame; kwargs...)\n\nPlot L2 approximation error vs polynomial degree with individual trial paths.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Must have columns :degree, :l2_error, :seed, :method\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\ndomain_filter::Union{Nothing, Float64}=nothing: Filter to specific domain\ntitle::String=\"L2 Approximation Error by Degree\": Plot title\nfig_size::Tuple{Int,Int}=(800, 500): Figure size\nshow_median::Bool=true: Overlay median line per method\ntrial_alpha::Float64=0.3: Alpha for individual trial lines\ncolors::Tuple=(Makie.wong_colors()[1], Makie.wong_colors()[2]): (standard, log) colors\n\nReturns\n\nFigure: Makie figure object\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_l2_convergence_trials"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_l2_error_evolution-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_l2_error_evolution(run; size=(800, 500))\n\nPlot mean and final L2 errors across episodes\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_l2_error_evolution"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_l2_trajectories-Tuple{Dict{String, Vector{Float64}}}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_l2_trajectories(trajectories; kwargs...)\n\nPlot L2 error trajectories for multiple policies.\n\nArguments\n\ntrajectories::Dict{String, Vector{Float64}}: Policy name → L2 error vector\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\ntitle::String = \"L2 Error Evolution\": Plot title\nyscale = log10: Y-axis scale (log10 or identity)\nxlabel::String = \"Step\": X-axis label\nylabel::String = \"L2 Error\": Y-axis label\nfig_size::Tuple{Int,Int} = (800, 500): Figure size\n\nReturns\n\nFigure: The Makie figure\n\nExample\n\ntrajectories = Dict(\n    \"AdaptiveL2\" => run_episode(env, AdaptiveL2Policy()).l2_trajectory,\n    \"GreedyDegree\" => run_episode(env, GreedyDegreePolicy()).l2_trajectory\n)\nfig = plot_l2_trajectories(trajectories)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_l2_trajectories"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_level_set-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_level_set(\n    formatted_data;\n    fig_size = (800, 600),\n    marker_size = 4,\n    title = \"Level Set Visualization\"\n)\n\nCreate a basic 3D scatter plot of level set points.\n\nArguments\n\nformatted_data: Output from to_makie_format\nfig_size: Figure dimensions\nmarker_size: Size of scatter markers\ntitle: Plot title\n\nReturns\n\nGLMakie Figure object\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_level_set"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_multi_strategy_comparison_simple-Tuple{Dict}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_multi_strategy_comparison_simple(results_dict;\n                                      expected_minima=5,\n                                      window_size=25)\n\nCompare multiple training strategies on same plot (simplified API).\n\nArguments\n\nresults_dict::Dict{String, NamedTuple}: Dict of strategy name => results\nexpected_minima::Int: Horizontal reference line\nwindow_size::Int: Rolling average window\n\nExample\n\nresults_dict = Dict(\n    \"DQN\" => run_dqn_training(),\n    \"Greedy\" => run_greedy_baseline(),\n    \"Random\" => run_random_baseline()\n)\nplot_multi_strategy_comparison_simple(results_dict)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_multi_strategy_comparison_simple"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_multifunction_learning_curves-Tuple{Dict{String, <:NamedTuple}}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_multifunction_learning_curves(data; action_data=nothing, window=50, size=(1600, 1000), ...)\n\nPlot per-function learning curves for multi-function RL training.\n\nShows 4-6 panels:\n\nSuccess rate vs episode (per function)\nAverage reward vs episode (per function)\nAverage steps vs episode (per function)\nFinal success rate bar chart\nPolicy evolution: subdivide ratio over time (if action_data provided)\nAction distribution stacked area chart (if action_data provided)\n\nArguments\n\ndata::Dict{String, NamedTuple}: Per-function training data with fields:\nepisode_numbers::Vector{Int}: Episode indices when function was sampled\nsuccess_rates::Vector{Float64}: Rolling success rate at each episode\nrewards::Vector{Float64}: Reward per episode\nsteps::Vector{Int}: Steps per episode\naction_data::NamedTuple=nothing: Policy evolution data from getactionevolution_data()\nwindow::Int=50: Rolling average window size for smoothing\nsize::Tuple{Int,Int}=(1600, 1000): Figure size\nshow_raw::Bool=true: Show raw data points (faint scatter)\ntitle::String=\"Per-Function Learning Curves\": Figure title\n\nReturns\n\nFigure: CairoMakie figure\n\nExample\n\nusing GlobtimPlots\n\n# After training with MultiEnv2D:\ndata = get_learning_curve_data(multi_env; window=50)\nfig = plot_multifunction_learning_curves(data)\nsave(\"learning_curves.pdf\", fig)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_multifunction_learning_curves"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_policy_evolution_comparison-Tuple{Vector}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_policy_evolution_comparison(runs::Vector; fig_size=(1400, 1000))\n\nCompare how different strategies evolve their action preferences across training.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_policy_evolution_comparison"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_predicate_pareto-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_predicate_pareto(df::DataFrame;\n                      x_col=:mean_evals, y_col=:mean_recovery,\n                      score_col=:pareto_score, label_col=nothing,\n                      front_col=nothing,\n                      title=\"Predicate sweep — evals/recovery Pareto\")\n    -> Figure\n\nScatter of predicate-sweep trials in the (cost, error) plane — both axes minimized — colored by score_col, with the Pareto front drawn as a staircase through the non-dominated points. If front_col names a Bool column, the front membership computed by the analyzer is used verbatim; otherwise the non-dominated set is derived here purely for display. label_col (optional) annotates front points.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_predicate_pareto"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_raw_vs_refined_eigenvalues-Tuple{Function, DataFrames.DataFrame, DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_raw_vs_refined_eigenvalues(f, df_raw, df_refined; sort_by=:euclidean_distance, fig_size=nothing)\n\nBefore/after BFGS comparison of eigenvalues at matched critical points. Sort options: :euclidean_distance, :function_value_diff, :eigenvalue_change.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_raw_vs_refined_eigenvalues"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_refinement_trajectories!-Tuple{Any, Vector{GlobtimPostProcessing.CriticalPointRefinementResult}, Vector{Vector{Float64}}}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_refinement_trajectories!(ax, refine_results, raw_points; kwargs...) -> Int\n\nOverlay refinement trajectories on an existing Axis.\n\nEach trajectory visualizes how a local solver (Newton / trust-region / NelderMead) moved a raw polynomial critical point toward the refined result.  Paths are drawn as colored lines from circle (start) to triangle (end), with intermediate iterates when the solver recorded a full trace.\n\nArguments\n\nax::Axis: Makie axis to draw on (mutated in place)\nrefine_results::Vector{CriticalPointRefinementResult}: Per-CP refinement results (must have .trace field — a Vector{Vector{Float64}} of iterates)\nraw_points::Vector{Vector{Float64}}: Starting points (same length & ordering as refine_results)\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nSelection — which trajectories to show\n\np_target::Union{Nothing, Vector{Float64}} = nothing: Sort raw CPs by distance to this point and show the n_show closest.  Mutually exclusive with indices.\nn_show::Int = 10: Number of trajectories to show when using p_target sorting.\nindices::Union{Nothing, Vector{Int}} = nothing: Explicit 1-based indices into refine_results / raw_points to plot.  Overrides p_target / n_show.\n\nProjection — for N-D problems\n\ndim_x::Int = 1: Parameter dimension to map to the x-axis.\ndim_y::Int = 2: Parameter dimension to map to the y-axis.\n\nClipping\n\nclip_bounds::Union{Nothing, Vector{Vector{Float64}}} = nothing: If provided, only draw trajectories that have at least one iterate inside this bounding box (format [[lo1, hi1], [lo2, hi2], ...]  — checked on dim_x and dim_y only).\n\nVisual style\n\nstyle::RefinementTrajectoryStyle = RefinementTrajectoryStyle(): Full style config.\nlabel::Union{String, Nothing} = \"refinement paths\": Legend label for the first trajectory group.  Pass nothing to suppress legend entries.\n\nReturns\n\nInt: Number of trajectories actually drawn.\n\nExample\n\nusing CairoMakie, GlobtimPlots\n\nfig = Figure()\nax = Axis(fig[1,1])\ncontourf!(ax, x_range, y_range, Z; colormap=:inferno)\n\nn_drawn = plot_refinement_trajectories!(ax, results, raw_cps;\n    p_target = p_true, n_show = 15,\n    style = RefinementTrajectoryStyle(linewidth=2.0))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_refinement_trajectories!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_state_action_heatmap-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_state_action_heatmap(state_action_pairs; fig_size=(1200, 800))\n\nHeatmap showing which actions are taken in which states. Requires state-action pair tracking during training.\n\nArguments\n\nstate_action_pairs: Vector of (state, action) tuples collected during episodes where state = [width, center, l2_error, degree, cond]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_state_action_heatmap"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_strategy_comparison-Tuple{Vector}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_strategy_comparison(runs::Vector; size=(1400, 1000))\n\nCompare multiple training runs (different strategies) on the same function\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_strategy_comparison"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_subdivision_error_heatmap-Tuple{Globtim.SubdivisionTree, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_subdivision_error_heatmap(\n    tree::SubdivisionTree, f;\n    resolution::Int = 200,\n    log_scale::Bool = true,\n    colormap::Symbol = :viridis,\n    show_boundaries::Bool = true,\n    boundary_color = :white,\n    boundary_width::Float64 = 1.0,\n    title::String = \"Polynomial Approximation Error\",\n    cp_points::Vector = Vector{Float64}[],\n    cp_types::Vector = String[],\n    raw_cp_points::Vector = Vector{Float64}[],\n    p_true = nothing,\n    style::SubdivisionPartitionStyle = SubdivisionPartitionStyle(),\n    fig = nothing,\n    ax = nothing,\n) → Figure\n\nCreate a 2D filled heatmap of |f(p) - poly(p)| across the subdivision domain, with subdomain boundaries overlaid.\n\nRequires the SubdivisionTree with populated polynomials (runtime only — polynomials are not serialized to JSON).\n\nArguments\n\ntree: The subdivision tree with polynomial approximations per leaf\nf: The objective function f(x::Vector{Float64}) → Float64\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nresolution: Grid points per axis (default 200)\nlog_scale: If true, plot log₁₀(error) (default true)\ncolormap: Makie colormap (default :viridis)\nshow_boundaries: Overlay subdomain boundaries (default true)\nboundary_color: Color for boundary lines (default :white)\nboundary_width: Line width for boundaries (default 1.0)\ntitle: Plot title\ncp_points, cp_types: Refined critical points and their types\nraw_cp_points: Raw (pre-refinement) critical points\np_true: True parameter vector\nstyle: SubdivisionPartitionStyle for CP marker styling\nfig, ax: Plot into existing Figure/Axis\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_subdivision_error_heatmap"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_subdivision_on_levelset-Tuple{Globtim.SubdivisionTree, Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_subdivision_on_levelset(tree::SubdivisionTree, f; kwargs...) → Figure\n\nPlot the objective function f as a filled contour (level set) with subdivision boundaries overlaid, colored by convergence status. Critical points and p* are scattered on top.\n\nRequires the SubdivisionTree and objective function to be in memory (runtime only).\n\nArguments\n\ntree: The subdivision tree (provides domain bounds and per-leaf L2 errors)\nf: The objective function f(x::Vector{Float64}) → Float64\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nresolution::Int = 200: Grid points per axis for contour evaluation\nn_levels::Int = 30: Number of contour levels\ncolormap::Symbol = :viridis: Colormap for the filled contour\nl2_tolerance: L2 tolerance for convergence border coloring\ncp_points, cp_types: Refined critical points and their types\nraw_cp_points: Raw (pre-refinement) critical points\np_true: True parameter vector\ntitle: Plot title\nstyle: SubdivisionPartitionStyle for marker/border styling\nfig, ax: Plot into existing Figure/Axis\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_subdivision_on_levelset"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_subdivision_on_levelset_from_bounds-Tuple{Any, Vector}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_subdivision_on_levelset_from_bounds(f, bounds; leaf_bounds, leaf_l2_errors, kwargs...) → Figure\n\nData-based version for when the tree is not available but leaf geometry and L2 errors have been extracted (e.g. from JSON results).\n\nArguments\n\nf: The objective function f(x::Vector{Float64}) → Float64\nbounds: Domain bounds [[x_lo, x_hi], [y_lo, y_hi]] or [(x_lo, x_hi), (y_lo, y_hi)]\nleaf_bounds: Per-leaf bounds [leaf][dim] → [lo, hi] or tuples\nleaf_l2_errors::Vector{Float64}: L2 error per leaf\n\nAll other keyword arguments are the same as the tree-based version.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_subdivision_on_levelset_from_bounds"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_subdivision_partition-Tuple{Vector, Vector{Float64}, Vector}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_subdivision_partition(leaf_bounds, leaf_l2_errors, leaf_degrees; kwargs...) → Figure\n\nCreate a domain partition visualization for a subdivision experiment result.\n\nArguments\n\nleaf_bounds::Vector: Per-leaf bounds, [leaf][dim] → [lo, hi]\nleaf_l2_errors::Vector{Float64}: L2 error per leaf\nleaf_degrees::Vector: Degree per leaf (Int or Vector{Int} for anisotropic)\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\ncp_points::Vector = []: Refined critical points (Vector{Float64}[])\ncp_types::Vector = []: CP type strings (\"min\"/\"saddle\"/\"max\")\nraw_cp_points::Vector = []: Raw (pre-refinement) critical points (Vector{Float64}[])\np_true = nothing: True parameter vector\nl2_tolerance = nothing: L2 tolerance for convergence border coloring\ncolorrange = nothing: Explicit (cmin, cmax) for color scale; auto-computed if nothing\ntitle::String = \"Domain Partition\": Plot title\nsubtitle::String = \"\": Plot subtitle\nstyle::SubdivisionPartitionStyle = SubdivisionPartitionStyle(): Styling config\nfig = nothing: Plot into existing Figure\nax = nothing: Plot into existing Axis\n\nReturns\n\nFigure: The Makie figure (backend-agnostic — display with GLMakie for interactive, save with CairoMakie)\n\nExample\n\nusing GlobtimPlots\nfig = plot_subdivision_partition(\n    leaf_bounds, leaf_l2_errors, leaf_degrees;\n    cp_points=cps, cp_types=types, p_true=[1.0, 1.5],\n    l2_tolerance=1e-4, title=\"LV2D subdivision\"\n)\nsave(\"partition.png\", fig; px_per_unit=2)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_subdivision_partition"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_subdivision_tree-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_subdivision_tree(tree; kwargs...) -> Figure\n\nCreate publication-quality visualization of a subdivision tree.\n\nArguments\n\ntree: SubdivisionTree from Globtim (uses duck typing)\n\nKeyword Arguments\n\nstyle::TreeVizStyle = TreeVizStyle(): Visual styling configuration\ntitle::String = \"\": Optional figure title\nshow_legend::Bool = true: Whether to show dimension color legend\nbalanced_layout::Bool = true: Use split-position-aware layout (recommended)\n\nReturns\n\nFigure: CairoMakie Figure object suitable for saving as PDF/SVG\n\nNotes\n\nAuto-scaling is enabled by default: node sizes, fonts, and figure dimensions adapt to tree size for optimal readability.\nSet style=TreeVizStyle(auto_scale=false, auto_fig_size=false) for fixed sizing.\n\nExample\n\nusing Globtim, GlobtimPlots\n\ntree = adaptive_refine(f, bounds, 4)  # uses default relative L2 tolerance of 0.03\nfig = plot_subdivision_tree(tree)\nsave(\"tree.pdf\", fig)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_subdivision_tree"},{"category":"function","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_theoretical_minimizer_distances","page":"API Reference","text":"Plot distance from theoretical minimizers to nearest computed critical points.\n\nFor each theoretical minimizer, computes the distance to the nearest critical point found by the polynomial method. Shows both average and maximum distances by degree.\n\nArguments\n\nresults: Dictionary mapping degrees to analysis results\ndf_theoretical_mins: DataFrame containing theoretical minimizer coordinates (x1, x2, ...)\nstart_degree: Minimum polynomial degree\nend_degree: Maximum polynomial degree\nstep: Step size between degrees (default: 1)\nshow_legend: Whether to display legend (default: true)\n\nReturns\n\nfig: Makie Figure object\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_theoretical_minimizer_distances"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_training_curves_simple-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_training_curves_simple(results;\n                             title=\"Training Progress\",\n                             expected_minima=nothing,\n                             window_size=25)\n\nPlot training curves from simple NamedTuple format (traindqnphase2.jl output).\n\nArguments\n\nresults: NamedTuple with fields:\nepisode_rewards::Vector{Float64}: Cumulative reward per episode\nepisode_minimizers::Vector{Float64}: Minimizers found per episode\nepisode_losses::Vector{Float64}: TD loss per episode (NaN if no training)\nfunc_config::Dict: Function metadata (for expected_minima)\n\nReturns\n\nfig::Figure: GLMakie figure (interactive window)\n\nExample\n\nusing GLMakie\nresults = include(\"examples/train_dqn_phase2.jl\")\nplot_training_curves_simple(results)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_training_curves_simple"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_training_progress-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_training_progress(run; size=(1200, 800))\n\nCreate multi-panel plot showing training progress:\n\nRewards per episode\nMinimizers found per episode\nSteps per episode\nFunction evaluations per episode\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_training_progress"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.plot_verdict_shares-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_verdict_shares(df::DataFrame;\n                    winner_col=:winner, family_col=:family,\n                    strat_cols=[:base_degree, :budget],\n                    title=\"Per-axis cut counterfactual — winner shares\")\n    -> Figure\n\nStacked-bar shares of counterfactual winners per stratum, one panel per value of family_col. Each row of df is one verdict record; winner_col values are \"per_axis\" / \"global\" / \"tie\". Strata are the distinct combinations of strat_cols within a family, labeled \"col=val col=val\" and annotated with the record count n.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.plot_verdict_shares"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.prepare_level_set_data-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{Array{StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, T}, 3}, Array{T}, T}} where T<:AbstractFloat","page":"API Reference","text":"prepare_level_set_data(\n    grid::Array{SVector{3,T},3},\n    values::Array{T},\n    level::T;\n    tolerance::T = T(0.01)\n) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nIdentify points in the grid that are close to the specified level.\n\nArguments\n\ngrid: 3D array of grid points\nvalues: Function values at each grid point\nlevel: Target level value\ntolerance: Maximum distance from level to include point\n\nReturns\n\nLevelSetData{T}: Container with filtered points and values\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.prepare_level_set_data"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.print_tree_summary-Tuple{Any}","page":"API Reference","text":"print_tree_summary(tree; io=stdout)\n\nPrint summary statistics for a subdivision tree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.print_tree_summary"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.rolling_mean-Tuple{Vector, Int64}","page":"API Reference","text":"Helper: Compute rolling mean with given window size\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.rolling_mean"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.save_plot-Tuple{Figure, String}","page":"API Reference","text":"save_plot(fig::Figure, output_path::String; format=:png)\n\nSave a Makie figure to file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.save_plot"},{"category":"function","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.split_position_label","page":"API Reference","text":"split_position_label(split_pos::Float64, width::Int=10) -> String\n\nCreate ASCII split position visualization: [—-|———]\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.split_position_label"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.to_makie_format-Union{Tuple{LevelSetData{T}}, Tuple{T}} where T<:AbstractFloat","page":"API Reference","text":"to_makie_format(level_set::LevelSetData{T}) where {T<:AbstractFloat}\n\nConvert LevelSetData to format suitable for Makie plotting.\n\nReturns\n\nNamed tuple with:\n\npoints: 3×N matrix of coordinates\nvalues: vector of function values\nxyz: tuple of (x, y, z) coordinate vectors\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.to_makie_format"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.tree_to_graph-Tuple{Vector{GlobtimPlots.SubdomainNodeInfo}}","page":"API Reference","text":"tree_to_graph(nodes::Vector{SubdomainNodeInfo}) -> SimpleDiGraph\n\nConvert extracted node info to Graphs.jl SimpleDiGraph.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.tree_to_graph"},{"category":"module","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots","page":"API Reference","text":"LV4D Plotting Module\n\nVisualization tools for Lotka-Volterra 4D parameter estimation experiments.\n\nThis module provides publication-quality plots for:\n\nConvergence rate analysis (log-log plots)\nDegree comparison plots\nDomain × degree heatmaps\n\nAll functions accept DataFrames from globtimpostprocessing analysis.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots._plot_convergence_line!-Tuple{Any, DataFrames.DataFrame, Symbol, Int64, Bool}","page":"API Reference","text":"Plot a convergence line for a single degree. Returns true if plot was added, false otherwise.\n\nArguments\n\nband_type::Symbol=:quantile: Type of uncertainty band:\n:quantile - IQR (25th-75th percentile) band\n:std - Mean ± standard deviation band\n:none - No band\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots._plot_convergence_line!"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_convergence_multi_degree-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_lv4d_convergence_multi_degree(df::DataFrame; gn_filter=nothing,\n                                   metric=:recovery_error, show_fit=true)\n\nPlot convergence for multiple degrees on a single log-log plot with rate annotations.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Data with domain, degree, and metric columns\ngn_filter: Optional GN value to filter by\nmetric::Symbol: Which metric to plot (:recoveryerror, :L2norm, :meanrecovery, :meanL2)\nshow_fit::Bool=true: Show fitted lines with slope annotations\n\nReturns\n\nFigure with multi-degree convergence plot.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_convergence_multi_degree"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_convergence_rate-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_lv4d_convergence_rate(df::DataFrame; metric=:recovery_error, gn_filter=nothing)\n\nPlot fitted convergence rate α (where error ∝ domain^α) vs degree.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Aggregated data with domain, degree columns\nmetric::Symbol: Which metric to compute rate for (:recoveryerror or :L2norm)\ngn_filter: Optional GN value to filter by\n\nReturns\n\nFigure showing convergence rate α per degree.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_convergence_rate"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_degree_comparison-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_lv4d_degree_comparison(df::DataFrame; domain_filter=nothing, gn_filter=nothing,\n                            metrics=[:mean_recovery, :mean_L2, :success_rate])\n\nMulti-panel plot comparing metrics across degrees for fixed domain.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Aggregated data with domain, degree, GN columns\ndomain_filter: Domain value to filter by (uses minimum if not specified)\ngn_filter: Optional GN value to filter by\nmetrics: Vector of metrics to plot (from aggregated columns)\n\nReturns\n\nFigure with one panel per metric.\n\nAvailable Metrics\n\nmeanrecovery: Mean ||pbest - ptrue|| / ||ptrue||\nmeanL2: Mean ||f - wd||_L2\nsuccessrate: Fraction with recoveryerror < 5%\nmeangradvalid: Mean gradient validation rate\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_degree_comparison"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_gn_comparison-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_lv4d_gn_comparison(df::DataFrame; domain_filter=nothing, degree_filter=nothing,\n                       metrics=[:mean_recovery, :success_rate])\n\nCompare metrics across different GN values.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Aggregated data with GN column\ndomain_filter: Domain value to filter by\ndegree_filter: Degree value to filter by\nmetrics: Vector of metrics to plot\n\nReturns\n\nFigure comparing GN values.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_gn_comparison"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_l2_by_degree-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_lv4d_l2_by_degree(df::DataFrame; gn_filter=nothing, domain_filter=nothing,\n                       show_fit=true, title=nothing)\n\nPlot L2 approximation error vs polynomial degree on log-linear scale.\n\nUse this plot when analyzing a single domain value to see how polynomial approximation improves with increasing degree.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Data with columns: domain, degree, GN, L2norm (or meanL2)\ngn_filter: Optional GN value to filter by\ndomain_filter: Optional domain value to filter by (uses minimum if not specified)\nshow_fit::Bool=true: Show fitted exponential decay line\ntitle: Optional custom title\n\nReturns\n\nFigure with degree on x-axis (linear), L2 error on y-axis (log).\n\nMetric Definition\n\nL2norm = ||f - wd||_L2 = polynomial approximation error\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_l2_by_degree"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_l2_convergence-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_lv4d_l2_convergence(df::DataFrame; gn_filter=nothing, degree_filter=nothing,\n                         show_fit=false, band_type=:quantile, title=nothing)\n\nPlot L2 approximation error vs domain size on log-log scale.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Data with columns: domain, degree, GN, L2norm (or meanL2)\ngn_filter: Optional GN value to filter by\ndegree_filter: Optional degree or range to filter by\nshow_fit::Bool=false: Show fitted convergence rate line\nband_type::Symbol=:quantile: Band type - :quantile (IQR 25-75%), :std, or :none\ntitle: Optional custom title\n\nReturns\n\nFigure with log-log convergence plot.\n\nMetric Definition\n\nL2norm = ||f - wd||_L2 = polynomial approximation error\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_l2_convergence"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_metrics_heatmap-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_lv4d_metrics_heatmap(df::DataFrame; metric=:success_rate, gn_filter=nothing,\n                          aggregation=:mean, show_n=true)\n\nHeatmap showing metric values across degree × domain grid.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Data with degree, domain columns (can be pre-aggregated with n_experiments)\nmetric::Symbol: Metric to display (e.g., :successrate, :meanrecovery, :mean_L2)\ngn_filter: Optional GN value to filter by\naggregation::Symbol: How to aggregate if multiple values (:mean, :max, :min)\nshow_n::Bool=true: Show experiment count (n=X) in each cell\n\nReturns\n\nFigure with heatmap visualization.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_metrics_heatmap"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_recovery_by_degree-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_lv4d_recovery_by_degree(df::DataFrame; gn_filter=nothing, domain_filter=nothing,\n                              show_fit=true, title=nothing)\n\nPlot parameter recovery error vs polynomial degree on log-linear scale.\n\nUse this plot when analyzing a single domain value to see how recovery error improves with increasing polynomial degree.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Data with columns: domain, degree, GN, recoveryerror (or meanrecovery)\ngn_filter: Optional GN value to filter by\ndomain_filter: Optional domain value to filter by (uses minimum if not specified)\nshow_fit::Bool=true: Show fitted exponential decay line\ntitle: Optional custom title\n\nReturns\n\nFigure with degree on x-axis (linear), recovery error on y-axis (log).\n\nMetric Definition\n\nrecoveryerror = ||pbest - ptrue|| / ||ptrue|| (relative parameter error)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_recovery_by_degree"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_recovery_convergence-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_lv4d_recovery_convergence(df::DataFrame; gn_filter=nothing, degree_filter=nothing,\n                               show_fit=false, band_type=:quantile, title=nothing)\n\nPlot parameter recovery error vs domain size on log-log scale.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Data with columns: domain, degree, GN, recoveryerror (or meanrecovery)\ngn_filter: Optional GN value to filter by\ndegree_filter: Optional degree or range to filter by\nshow_fit::Bool=false: Show fitted convergence rate line\nband_type::Symbol=:quantile: Band type - :quantile (IQR 25-75%), :std, or :none\ntitle: Optional custom title\n\nReturns\n\nFigure with log-log convergence plot.\n\nMetric Definition\n\nrecoveryerror = ||pbest - ptrue|| / ||ptrue|| (relative parameter error)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_lv4d_recovery_convergence"},{"category":"method","location":"api.html#GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_parameter_comparison-Tuple{Vector, Vector}","page":"API Reference","text":"plot_parameter_comparison(p_true, p_estimated; labels, title)\n\nSide-by-side bar plot comparing true vs estimated parameters.\n\nArguments\n\np_true::Vector: True parameter values\np_estimated::Vector: Estimated parameter values\nlabels::Vector{String}: Parameter labels (default: [\"α\", \"β\", \"γ\", \"δ\"])\ntitle::String: Plot title\n\nReturns\n\nFigure with grouped bar chart comparing true vs estimated parameters.\n\nExample\n\nfig = plot_parameter_comparison([0.2, 0.3, 0.5, 0.6], [0.201, 0.299, 0.502, 0.598])\nsave(\"comparison.png\", fig)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"GlobtimPlots.LV4DPlots.plot_parameter_comparison"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Migration-Guide","page":"Migration Guide","text":"This guide helps you migrate from using plotting functions in the main Globtim package to using GlobtimPlots.jl.","title":"Migration Guide"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Quick-Migration","page":"Migration Guide","text":"","title":"Quick Migration"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Before-(Globtim)","page":"Migration Guide","text":"using Globtim\nusing CairoMakie\n\n# Plotting functions were part of Globtim\nplot_polyapprox_levelset(poly, input)","title":"Before (Globtim)"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#After-(GlobtimPlots)","page":"Migration Guide","text":"using GlobtimPlots\nusing CairoMakie  # Load the backend\n\n# Same function names, now in dedicated package\nplot_polyapprox_levelset(poly, input) ","title":"After (GlobtimPlots)"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Key-Changes","page":"Migration Guide","text":"Separate Package: Plotting functions are now in a dedicated package\nExtension System: Backend packages (CairoMakie, GLMakie) are loaded as extensions\nSame API: Function names and signatures remain unchanged\nCleaner Dependencies: Main optimization code no longer depends on plotting packages","title":"Key Changes"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Migration-Phases","page":"Migration Guide","text":"Based on the complexity assessment, migrate in this order:","title":"Migration Phases"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Phase-1:-Low-Complexity-Functions","page":"Migration Guide","text":"Statistical plotting functions\nBasic 2D level set plots  \nConvergence analysis plots","title":"Phase 1: Low Complexity Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Phase-2:-Medium-Complexity-Functions","page":"Migration Guide","text":"3D surface visualization\nInteractive level sets\nEigenvalue analysis plots","title":"Phase 2: Medium Complexity Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Phase-3:-High-Complexity-Functions","page":"Migration Guide","text":"Animation systems\nInteractive algorithm tracking\nReal-time convergence monitoring\nTightly coupled mathematical visualizations","title":"Phase 3: High Complexity Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Common-Migration-Issues","page":"Migration Guide","text":"","title":"Common Migration Issues"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Extension-Loading","page":"Migration Guide","text":"Make sure to load the appropriate backend:\n\nusing GlobtimPlots\nusing CairoMakie  # For static plots\n# or\nusing GLMakie     # For interactive plots","title":"Extension Loading"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Data-Structure-Compatibility","page":"Migration Guide","text":"The package expects the same data structures:\n\nApproxPoly{T,S} - Polynomial approximation data\nTestInput - Problem domain configuration\nDataFrame - Critical points and analysis results  \nLevelSetData{T} - Level set visualization data","title":"Data Structure Compatibility"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Coordinate-Transformations","page":"Migration Guide","text":"Coordinate transformation utilities should be handled by your data preparation code before calling plotting functions.","title":"Coordinate Transformations"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Testing-Your-Migration","page":"Migration Guide","text":"Install GlobtimPlots: using Pkg; Pkg.add(url=\"https://github.com/gescholt/GlobtimPlots.jl\")\nLoad appropriate backend: using CairoMakie or using GLMakie\nTest basic plotting: using GlobtimPlots; # your plotting code\nRun your existing test suite to ensure compatibility","title":"Testing Your Migration"},{"category":"section","location":"migration.html#Getting-Help","page":"Migration Guide","text":"If you encounter issues during migration:\n\nCheck that the appropriate backend is loaded\nVerify your data structures match the expected formats\nConsult the API documentation for function signatures\nOpen an issue on the GitHub repository","title":"Getting Help"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#GlobtimPlots.jl","page":"Home","text":"A Julia package for advanced plotting and visualization of global optimization algorithms and polynomial approximations.","title":"GlobtimPlots.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Overview","page":"Home","text":"GlobtimPlots.jl provides a comprehensive suite of plotting functions for:\n\nLevel Set Visualization: Interactive and static level set plots\n3D Surface Plots: Advanced 3D surface visualization with rotation and animation\nConvergence Analysis: Statistical analysis and visualization of algorithm convergence\nEigenvalue Analysis: Specialized plots for Hessian eigenvalues and condition numbers\nError Function Visualization: 1D and 2D error function plots with critical points","title":"Overview"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Gallery","page":"Home","text":"Sample outputs regenerated by examples/gallery.jl:\n\nPolynomial approximation level set — cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset on the Camel function:\n\n(Image: Camel level-set with critical points)\n\nAdaptive subdivision partition — plot_subdivision_partition on an anisotropic test function (high frequency in x1, low frequency in x2). The algorithm subdivides only along x_1; color encodes log10 L2 error per leaf:\n\n(Image: Anisotropic subdivision)\n\nConvergence vs polynomial degree — Camel degree sweep with L2 approximation error (log, left axis) and number of recovered critical points (right axis). Both pivot dramatically between degree 4 and degree 6:\n\n(Image: Camel — L2 error and CP count vs degree)\n\nMorse spectrum at each critical point — Hessian eigenvalues as a vertical segment from λ₁ to λ₂, colored by Morse classification. Minima above y=0 (positive definite), maxima below (negative definite), saddles cross the Morse threshold:\n\n(Image: Camel — full Hessian spectrum)","title":"Gallery"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Features","page":"Home","text":"","title":"Features"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Static-Plotting-(CairoMakie-Backend)","page":"Home","text":"High-quality publication-ready plots\nLevel set visualization\nConvergence analysis plots\nStatistical distribution plots\nEigenvalue spectrum analysis","title":"Static Plotting (CairoMakie Backend)"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Interactive-Plotting-(GLMakie-Backend)","page":"Home","text":"Real-time 3D surface visualization\nInteractive level sets\nAnimation sequences\nCamera flyover animations\nReal-time algorithm tracking","title":"Interactive Plotting (GLMakie Backend)"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Installation","page":"Home","text":"GlobtimPlots is not yet registered in the General registry; install it (and a Makie backend) from its public repository:\n\nusing Pkg\nPkg.add(url=\"https://github.com/gescholt/GlobtimPlots.jl\")\nPkg.add(\"CairoMakie\")   # static backend; or GLMakie for interactive windows","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Quick-Start","page":"Home","text":"Load a Makie backend (CairoMakie for static files, GLMakie for interactive windows) before any plot call, then render a polynomial level set with its critical points:\n\nusing Globtim, GlobtimPlots\nusing CairoMakie\nusing DynamicPolynomials: @polyvar\nusing HomotopyContinuation   # enables the :hc critical-point solver\n\n# 1. Approximate a test function and solve for its critical points (Globtim)\nTR  = TestInput(camel; dim=2, center=[0.0, 0.0], GN=200, sample_range=5.0)\npol = Constructor(TR, 6, basis=:chebyshev, precision=RationalPrecision)\n@polyvar x[1:2]\ndf_cp = process_crit_pts(solve_polynomial_system(x, pol), camel, TR)\ndf_cp, df_min = analyze_critical_points(camel, df_cp, TR; tol_dist=0.00125)\n\n# 2. Plot the level set with critical points overlaid (GlobtimPlots)\napol = adapt_polynomial_data(pol)\nainp = adapt_problem_input(TR)\nfig  = cairo_plot_polyapprox_levelset(apol, ainp, df_cp, df_min; title=\"Six-hump camel\")\nCairoMakie.save(\"camel_levelset.png\", fig)\n\nThis is the recipe used to generate the gallery image above; the full version with the Morse spectrum, subdivision partition, and convergence sweep lives in pkg/globtimplots/examples/gallery.jl.","title":"Quick Start"},{"category":"section","location":"index.html#Migration-from-Globtim","page":"Home","text":"This package extracts plotting functionality from the main Globtim package to provide:\n\nCleaner separation of concerns  \nReduced dependencies in core optimization code\nExtensible plotting system\nBetter maintainability\n\nSee the Migration Guide for detailed migration instructions.","title":"Migration from Globtim"}]
}
